  "mechanisms": [
    "Irrelevant speech automatically captures attentional resources, impairing the processing of visually presented items.",
    "Reduced theta activity reflects a withdrawal of attentional resources from to-be-remembered items, impacting working memory.",
    "Interference with the phonological loop (Baddeley's model).",
    "Disruption of order information by coexisting order information from changing-state irrelevant sound (Jones' O-OER model).",
    "Reduction of overall available attentional resources (Neath's feature model)."
  ],
  "moderators": [],
  "implementation_implications": [
    "The findings suggest that environments with changing-state irrelevant speech can detrimentally affect cognitive performance by reducing attentional resources and impairing working memory processes, even when the sound is not task-related and subjects are told to ignore it."
  ],
  "domains": [
    "A5_Acoustic",
